From 2aaf60fb74796de8afdbb74cfb6c662350cd251b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 18:50:20 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Drones: electronic warfare drones change their target's
 attributes

Painters, sensor dampeners and tracking disruptors apply their own attributes to the target while
working (signatureRadiusBonus; maxTargetRange/scanResolution multipliers; tracking/maxRange/falloff
multipliers on an NPC or on a ship's turrets), recorded per drone and undone in StopEwar(), which
StopWeb() now calls, so every existing stop path (new order, target change, recall, release, death)
removes them.  Neutralizers drain energyDestabilizationAmount from the target's capacitor each cycle.
NPCAIMgr::RefreshWeaponStats() re-reads the NPC's cached signature radius, optimal, falloff and tracking
after a change.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GZgkReFMTa8JWavQEivVUA
---
